          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong cellular approximation theorem
            states that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complexes"} CW complexes
            (with chosen CW presentations) is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
            to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+map"} cellular map
            = succeed "-structure," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-skeleta"} n-skeleta
            to
            = succeed "-skeleta" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            This is the analogue for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+approximation+theorem"} simplicial approximation theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realizations"} geometric realizations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
            to a map induced by a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            (after subdivision).
          %h2#statement Statement
          #CellularApproximationTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon (X, A) \to (X', A')
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+CW-complexes"} relative CW-complexes
              that is cellular on a subcomplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, B)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon (X, A) \to (X', A')
              that is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              relative to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p It follows that if two cellular maps between CW-complexes are homotopic, then they are so by a cellular homotopy.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Spanier66"}> Spanier 66, p. 404
            , review in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#May99"} May 99, Section 10.4
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"} Hatcher 02, Thm. 4.8
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#FiniteDimensionalUniversalBundles Finite-dimensional universal bundles
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a suitable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E G \to B G
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            equipped with some
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannians"} Grassmannians
          %p
            Then the cellular approximation theorem (Thm.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellularApproximationTheorem"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi d
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_d G
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E G
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            to its
